<main class="max-w-5xl m-auto pt-16 pb-8 overflow-clip">
    <div class="sm:flex sm:flex-wrap">
        <div class="sm:basis-[50%] p-8">
            <div class="headline-4">Open Source Vario.</div>
            <p>
                Leaf is a powerful flight computer in a tiny package - small enough to strap to a riser, but crammed full of capability.
            </p>
            <p><br>
                All valuable flight information is shown on screen, and behind the scenes Leaf will log your data and flight tracks to the included 8GB SD card in IGC format.
            </p>
            <p><br>
                While Leaf is a complete flight computer package, you can also pair to other devices with Bluetooth and WiFi to expand even further.
            </p>
            <p><br>
                Leaf is designed to mount anywhere: attach to a riser or harness strap, mount to a flight deck, or use the included snap-in base plate for even more mounting options (velcro strap and safety lanyard included).
            </p>
            <p><br>
                Best of all, Leaf is Open Source, and will be constantly improving with community input and feedback.  Feel free to share your ideas!
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="sm:basis-[50%] sm:border-l border-l-gray-300 p-8">
            <div class="headline-5">Features</div>
            <ul class="pl-8">
                <li>All flight information on a sunlight-readable screen (even with polarized sunglasses) including vario, altitude, GPS track and speed, glide ratio, wind estimates, and more!</li>
                <li>Instant vario response with combined barometer, accelerometer and gyro sensing</li>
                <li>Automatic IGC flight logging to the SD card</li>
                <li>Web App for managing logs, profiles, waypoints, and routes from a phone or laptop</li>
                <li>Mount on a riser, harness, or flight deck with the included strap, lanyard, or base plate</li>
                <li>Bluetooth and WiFi for device pairing, web tools, and easy firmware updates</li>
                <li>20 hour battery life.  USB-C charge port</li>
                <li>Replaceable screen, battery, and case</li>
                <li>100% open source hardware and software, improved with community ideas and feedback</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</main>
